.TH TINYDNS-GET 1 "2026-07-23" "rgbdns 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tinydns-get \- inspect an answer from tinydns source data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tinydns-get
.I type name
.RI [ client-ip ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads
.I data
from the current directory, evaluates a query without starting a server, and
prints the decoded response. The optional address controls client-location
selection.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tinydns (1),
.BR tinydns-data (1)
